# ActivationManager — License/Copy Protection System
# Files: src/coordinator/ActivationManager.h, ActivationManager.cpp
# Related: data/register.html, data/script.js (checkLicenseAndNavigate), keygen.py

## PURPOSE
Challenge-response license system. Device code derived from MAC, keys validated via CRC32.

## LICENSE TIERS
- FREE: 20h playtime (1200 minutes)
- EXTENDED: 80h playtime (4800 minutes) — TIME- key
- FULL: unlimited — FULL- key

## DEVICE CODE
- Derived from last 3 bytes of WiFi MAC address
- Encoded with DEVICE_CODE_ALPHABET (22 chars, no I/O/L/Z)
- Format: "XX XX XX" (6 chars + 2 spaces)
- Cached after first generation

## KEY GENERATION (generateKey)
- Input: prefix ("FULL-" or "TIME-") + cleanDeviceCode + salt
- Hash: ~esp_rom_crc32_le(~0U, data, len) — standard CRC32, matches Python zlib.crc32()
- Result: hash % 1000000000, formatted as 9-digit string with leading zeros

## VALIDATION
- On boot: loadLicense() reads /license.json from LittleFS
- validateLicense() generates expected keys, compares with stored keys
- FULL checked first, then EXTENDED, else FREE

## REGISTRATION
- attemptRegistration(key): 9-char key, checks against FULL then TIME expected keys
- On match: saves to /license.json, updates status

## DEBUG MODE (PUCK_RACER_DEBUG)
- setDebugTimeLimits(free_mins, extended_mins): override limits for testing
- applyTimeExtensionKey(): auto-apply TIME key without user input
- API: POST /api/license/debug, GET /api/license/apply_time_key
- Backend routes in WebHandler.cpp are behind #if defined(PUCK_RACER_DEBUG)

### Enabling debug mode in platformio.ini
For local development/testing, add the flag back to [env:coordinator] build_flags:
```ini
build_flags =
    -D PUCK_RACER_DEBUG
    -DBOARD_HAS_PSRAM
    -mfix-esp32-psram-cache-issue
```
Remove it again before building release binaries for the web flasher.
The release build process (merge_bin) is documented below.

## FRONTEND CHECK (data/script.js)
- checkLicenseAndNavigate(url): fetches /api/license
- If status != FULL AND playtime expired → 30s countdown overlay (showLicenseCountdown)
- Overlay: countdown, register link, auto-navigates to game after 30s. Currently only used in React2P

## KEYGEN (keygen.py)
- Python script generating keys from device code
- Uses zlib.crc32() — matches ESP32 implementation

## REMOVED DEBUG UI (register.html) — for re-adding during testing
The following was removed from register.html for release. Backend routes are already
behind #if defined(PUCK_RACER_DEBUG) in WebHandler.cpp — this is the frontend counterpart.

### HTML (insert before </main> closing tag):
```html
<!-- DEBUG SECTION -->
<div class="card" id="debug-section" style="display: none; border-color: var(--danger); margin-top: 20px;">
    <h2 style="color: var(--danger);">Debug & Test-Optionen</h2>
    <p class="license-info">
        Mit diesen Optionen kannst du die Zeitlimits für die Lizenzsperre zu Testzwecken manipulieren.
    </p>
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 15px;">
        <div>
            <label for="debug-free-mins">Test-Limit (Minuten)</label>
            <input type="number" id="debug-free-mins" value="1200">
        </div>
        <div>
            <label for="debug-extended-mins">Erweitertes Limit (Minuten)</label>
            <input type="number" id="debug-extended-mins" value="4800">
        </div>
    </div>
    <button id="debug-set-times" class="btn-warn">Debug-Zeiten setzen</button>
    <hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); margin: 20px 0;">
    <button id="debug-apply-time-key" class="btn-primary" style="background: var(--success);">Simuliere "+60h" Key</button>
</div>
```

### JavaScript (insert at end of DOMContentLoaded callback, before closing `});`):
```javascript
// --- DEBUG LOGIC ---
const urlParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
if (urlParams.get('debug') === '1') {
    const debugSection = document.getElementById('debug-section');
    debugSection.style.display = 'block';

    document.getElementById('debug-set-times').addEventListener('click', () => {
        const free_mins = document.getElementById('debug-free-mins').value;
        const extended_mins = document.getElementById('debug-extended-mins').value;
        
        fetch('/api/license/debug', {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },
            body: `free_mins=${free_mins}&extended_mins=${extended_mins}`
        }).then(res => {
            if(res.ok) {
                showMessage('Debug-Zeiten wurden gesetzt. Seite neu laden.', 'success', 4000);
                setTimeout(() => location.reload(), 1500);
            } else {
                showMessage('Fehler beim Setzen der Debug-Zeiten.', 'error');
            }
        });
    });

    document.getElementById('debug-apply-time-key').addEventListener('click', () => {
        fetch('/api/license/apply_time_key')
            .then(res => {
                if(res.ok) {
                    showMessage('Zeit-Schlüssel simuliert. Seite wird neu geladen.', 'success', 4000);
                    setTimeout(() => location.reload(), 1500);
                } else {
                    showMessage('Konnte Schlüssel nicht anwenden (Vollversion schon aktiv?).', 'error');
                }
            });
    });
}
```

### Activation: open /register.html?debug=1
### Requires: PUCK_RACER_DEBUG defined in firmware build for backend routes to exist

## RELEASE BUILD PROCESS (web flasher binaries)
1. Remove `-D PUCK_RACER_DEBUG` from platformio.ini [env:coordinator] build_flags
2. Compile: `pio run -e coordinator` and `pio run -e puck`
3. Build LittleFS: `pio run -t buildfs -e coordinator`
4. Merge coordinator (ESP32-S3, 16MB):
   ```
   esptool.exe --chip esp32s3 merge-bin -o webseite/bin/coordinator.bin \
       --flash-mode dio --flash-freq 80m --flash-size 16MB \
       0x0     .pio/build/coordinator/bootloader.bin \
       0x8000  .pio/build/coordinator/partitions.bin \
       0x10000 .pio/build/coordinator/firmware.bin \
       0x610000 .pio/build/coordinator/littlefs.bin
   ```
5. Merge puck (ESP32-C3, 4MB):
   ```
   esptool.exe --chip esp32c3 merge-bin -o webseite/bin/puck.bin \
       --flash-mode dio --flash-freq 80m --flash-size 4MB \
       0x0     .pio/build/puck/bootloader.bin \
       0x8000  .pio/build/puck/partitions.bin \
       0x10000 .pio/build/puck/firmware.bin
   ```
6. Update version in webseite/bin/coordinator_manifest.json and puck_manifest.json
7. Update version tables in webseite/flasher.html and webseite/downloads.html
